messages:
Miriam L: Heads-up — I reproduced a tiny duplicated fragment at the head of resumed SSE payloads in the browser polyfill after auth refresh. Repro is consistent: 3-6 chars of the previous chunk reappear.

Devon R: Native EventSource or our polyfill? Which browsers?

Miriam L: Polyfill, Chrome + Safari. Native ES seems fine. Repro steps: start streaming, wait for short JWT to expire, SDK refreshes token and reconnects, server resumes from last-id, UI shows overlap like `...pqrs` then `pqrsTUVW`.

Sam K: Sounds like parse buffer state surviving reconnect. Node SDK clears parser on reconnect; browser polyfill currently preserves an unfinished buffer to avoid dropping fragments. If server resumes inclusive of the last byte we get duplicated chars.

Kevin P: Ops note — reverse proxy idle closes sometimes happen mid-frame which can leave a partial fragment in memory. nginx with low keepalive_timeout reproduces this.

Miriam L: Snippet from the polyfill parse loop that probably causes it:
```
let buf = '';
polyfill.ondata = (chunk) => {
  buf += chunk;
  const blocks = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = blocks.pop() || '';
  for (const b of blocks) handleEventBlock(b);
};
// reconnect today preserves buf
```

Devon R: Two straightforward mitigations: clear buf on reconnect (client-side) OR change resume semantics server-side to be exclusive (start AFTER last delivered byte). Ideally both.

Sam K: For parity we should normalize resume headers (support Last-Event-ID header and resume_token query param on both SDKs) and implement client-side dedupe by sequence id so duplicate bytes are ignored.

ops-bot: Reminder — staging nginx has 60s idle timeout which can cause mid-chunk closures during stress tests.

Miriam L: I'll open a tiny PR that clears the parse buffer on reconnect, adds an opt-in config resumeStrategy=("exclusive"|"inclusive") defaulting to "exclusive", and includes a unit test that simulates a TCP close mid-chunk. Filing issue #4229 with traces and repro script.

Kevin P: Also recommend adding server keepalive heartbeats (eg server sends ":hb\n\n" every 20s). Ensure heartbeats are ignored by the renderer and not billed. Ops can provide an nginx example to avoid mid-chunk closes.

Sam K: Short-term fallback: if resume fails repeatedly, SDK should switch to short polling for that conversation to avoid repeated visual duplicates.

ci-bot: started CI for branch fix/sse-polyfill-buffer (build 6210) :rocket:

Devon R: Action items:
- Miriam: PR to clear buffer on reconnect, resumeStrategy opt, unit + e2e for mid-chunk close
- Sam: spec doc for resume header parity and client dedupe by seq
- Kevin: ops example nginx config + keepalive recommendation

Miriam L: Will tag reviewers. Will close once CI green and e2e passes. :white_check_mark:
